{"name":"Hereford Bull","hex":"#5f3b36","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An adult male, specifically:\n An adult male of domesticated cattle or oxen.","An adult male of domesticated cattle or oxen."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Large and strong, like a bull.","Of large mammals, adult male."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bull"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hereford cattle","blocks":[{"text":"The Hereford is a British breed of beef cattle originally from Herefordshire in the West Midlands of England. It was the result of selective breeding from the mid-eighteenth century by a few families in Herefordshire, beginning some decades before the noted work of Robert Bakewell."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Hereford_cow%2C_Souris%2C_Prince_Edward_Island.jpg/330px-Hereford_cow%2C_Souris%2C_Prince_Edward_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hereford_cattle","wikidata":"Q737173"},{"title":"Hereford","blocks":[{"text":"Hereford is a cathedral city and the county town of the ceremonial county of Herefordshire, England. It is on the banks of the River Wye and lies 16 miles (26 km) east of the border with Wales, 23 miles (37 km) north-west of Gloucester and 24 miles (39 km) south-west of Worcester. With a population of 61,900 in 2024, it is the largest settlement in Herefordshire."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Centre_of_Hereford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4306743.jpg/330px-Centre_of_Hereford_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4306743.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hereford","wikidata":"Q204720"},{"title":"Bull","blocks":[{"text":"A bull is an intact adult male of the species Bos taurus (cattle). More muscular and aggressive than the females of the same species, bulls have long been an important symbol in many religions, including for sacrifices. These animals play a significant role in beef ranching, dairy farming, and a variety of sporting and cultural activities, including bullfighting and bull riding."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/A_Friesian_Bull%2C_Llandeilo_Graban_-_geograph.org.uk_-_579885.jpg/330px-A_Friesian_Bull%2C_Llandeilo_Graban_-_geograph.org.uk_-_579885.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bull","wikidata":"Q693690"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Illustrirte_Zeitung_%281843%29_12_184_1_Hereford-Bulle_des_Herrn_Jeffries.PNG/500px-Illustrirte_Zeitung_%281843%29_12_184_1_Hereford-Bulle_des_Herrn_Jeffries.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Illustrirte_Zeitung_%281843%29_12_184_1_Hereford-Bulle_des_Herrn_Jeffries.PNG/500px-Illustrirte_Zeitung_%281843%29_12_184_1_Hereford-Bulle_des_Herrn_Jeffries.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bull of Mr. Jeffries, winner of first prize of the Royal Agricultural Show in Derby in 1843","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIllustrirte_Zeitung_(1843)_12_184_1_Hereford-Bulle_des_Herrn_Jeffries.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Hereford_cattle_in_Quebec_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Hereford_cattle_in_Quebec_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Hereford_cattle_in_Quebec_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Hereford_cattle_in_Quebec_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Hereford_cattle_in_Quebec_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Hereford_cattl